    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Headmaster:\u200b</strong>\u200b &quot;Congratulations, Class. You've graduated. But you will <i>not</i> leave this school. The year is 2033 AD. Outside these walls, 30 billion souls fight over scraps in a world that collapsed three years ago. You are not saviors; you are burdens. Society cannot bear you.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\u200b<strong>\u200bHowever...\u200b</strong>\u200b The Human Purification Act grants <i>one</i> student from Class A the privilege \u2013 or curse \u2013 of stepping into the desolation. Only the most exceptional may pass. The rest? They will remain here forever... preserved as perfect specimens of a lost generation.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\u200b<strong>\u200bSo fight.\u200b</strong>\u200b Claw your way to the top. Prove you are worthy of survival. Prove you are the <i>one</i>.&quot;</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\u200b<strong>\u200bExperience the Brutal Elegance of [</strong>Graduation Game<strong>] - A Unique 4-Player Battle Royale\u200b</strong>\u200b</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\u200b<strong>\u200bSurvive the Last School Standing:\u200b</strong>\u200b Trapped in your crumbling alma mater, compete against three classmates in a high-stakes struggle for the sole escape.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\u200b<strong>\u200bDeception is Your Weapon :\u200b</strong>\u200b Forge alliances, break promises, and outwit rivals. Built-in voice chat fuels the tension \u2013 trust is fleeting, betrayal is survival.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\u200b<strong>\u200bPlay Your Way:\u200b</strong>\u200b Jump into existing sessions or create your own private room to invite friends into this desperate graduation ceremony.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\u200b<strong>\u200bBecome the Exemplar... or the Exhibit:\u200b</strong>\u200b Will you earn the right to face the horrors outside, or will you become a permanent, pristine relic of the past?</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\u200b<strong>\u200bThe Ultimate Question: Are You Exceptional Enough to Deserve the World?\u200b</strong>\u200b</p>",
